     I never claimed that any random deletion takes place.
When you first enter a level for which a bones file exists,
there is a random chance that it will be loaded (which you
snipped out of my earlier post), with the alternative being
an ordinary new level.  So it is entirely possible to pass
a deadly bones level by luck (player's luck, not in-game
Luck).  The bones file will still be present for the next
character who reaches that depth, and it may or may not get
loaded then.

     When you enter a level and an existing bones files is
loaded, that file is deleted immediately and the game then
forgets the fact that it was ever a bones level.  If the
new character dies on that same level, the normal random
chance for saving a bones file is used.  On deeper levels,
that chance is high and the odds for a double, triple, &c
bones becomes likely; at shallow levels, it's much less
likely.  And there is always some chance that the game ends
without saving any bones regardless of depth.  So there is
a random chance that a bones file will go away when someone
dies there.  But it's not random deletion; the deletion is
absolutely certain and the chance for saving a replacement
is random.


